format session-log-v1
stamp 20260819.130844
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan regions -- declared sharing, W xor X held structurally
prompt Autonomous loop lap -- Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat; the prior lap recommended the memory-region ring or the declarative Brix/Bron system description.
think Standfast first -- walked crux/REDS.md: living rows 80-87 all read CLOSED or released, nothing agent-closable open. Line clear, constructive work may begin.
think Rota lap 20 of 27 -- deep-read context/QUIN.md. Quin keeps the fifth OS variant and the inference Q-vane; the four voices (Lattice, Scribble, Lantern, Ember) are carried by Kyri, and the report-never-urge practice governs the close of this lap.
think Chose the memory-region ring over the declarative system description, crux-first: a description that names the whole static architecture wants all three primitives declared beneath it. Capabilities and channels stood; regions was the missing leg. The description round becomes cheaper and truer once it has three real things to describe.
think Shaped the ring against the Microkit clean-room brief -- regions explicitly declared and explicitly mapped, granted to named domains with named permissions, sharing deliberate and visible rather than ambient. Kept the concept, wrote our own Rye; no source crossed the clean room.
think Chose two load-bearing invariants rather than a permission bitmask. Every grant reads, since a grant permitting nothing declares nothing. And write never stands beside execute in one grant -- the W xor X rule, asserted at Grant.init and refused by name at the door, so the property is structural rather than remembered.
think Named six refusals so the map can audit itself -- no_such_region, no_such_domain, not_granted, write_denied, execute_denied, allowed. A bare no covers five different situations, and a map that cannot say which one cannot be reviewed.
think Added two summarizing reads a human can check a declaration by: holders counts how widely one region is shared, footprint sums the bytes one domain reaches across every grant. Both bounded, both asserted.
think Ran the tame style check after the first GREEN -- bans clean, yet run_self_test printed at 89 lines on the length ratchet. Turned the ratchet in the same round: split into check_declared_access, check_reads, check_refusals, each with its own contract assert. Second run no longer names the file.
obs The witness went GREEN on the first build, so I proved the RED path before trusting it -- removed the WriteExecute guard, rebuilt to a scratch binary, and watched Grant.init's own legality assert abort the run (exit 134). Defense in depth confirmed: the door refuses, and the constructor asserts. Scratch binary removed, tree restored, both caravan witnesses re-GREEN.
obs The version constant first carried a stamp ahead of the live clock; read TZ=America/New_York date and corrected it to 20260819.130844 before the send. A fabricated stamp is a red even when it is only a string.
obs Kept the ring self-contained rather than importing channels.rye's roster. One shared roster would be the truer composition eventually; the happy zone wins for now -- a fast isolated test, no build coupling, and the declarative system description is the round where the three rings genuinely converge.
loom witness=caravan_regions_witness domains=4 regions=4 grants=7 checks=44 build_ok=1
file caravan/regions.rye the memory-region ring -- declared regions, named grants, six refusals, W xor X, holders and footprint
file tools/caravan_regions_witness.rish builds and runs the self-test, asserting GREEN and the W xor X report line
file caravan/README.md the module roster gains regions, and a new section names why sharing is granted rather than assumed
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge refreshed to the region ring; git nib pinned in the same commit
recommend keep-going -- the three primitives now stand, so the declarative Brix/Bron system description is the next crux: one bounded declaration naming domains, channels, regions, and grants, parsed and asserted, with a witness that proves the graph whole. No key, no funds.
